                                    <h1>Amazon Great Indian Sale Marketing Playbook for D2C 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Amazon Great Indian Sale (GIS) is Amazon India's biggest annual sale event — typically Diwali-adjacent (October) + drives 20-40% of Amazon India revenue for participating D2C brands in 4-7 day window. Combined with Prime Day (July) + Flipkart Big Billion Days competition. Here is the complete playbook.</p>
                                    <h2>Amazon Great Indian Sale Timeline</h2>
                                    <p>GIS typically 4-7 days late September / early October (Diwali-adjacent).<br><strong>8-12 weeks before:</strong> inventory + creative + campaign planning + Amazon account manager coordination.<br><strong>4-6 weeks before:</strong> creative + Sponsored Products campaigns + A+ content preparation.<br><strong>2-3 weeks before:</strong> full campaign launch + pre-GIS teaser deals.<br><strong>GIS 4-7 day period:</strong> peak revenue + campaign monitoring + inventory management.<br><strong>Post-GIS:</strong> follow-through Diwali + Dhanteras + festive extension.</p>
                                    <h2>Category-Specific GIS Playbook</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Consumer electronics:</strong> Peak category — deepest discounts + volume expected.<br><strong>Fashion + apparel:</strong> Festive collections + Diwali outfit push.<br><strong>Home + furniture:</strong> Diwali home refresh + festive decor.<br><strong>Beauty + personal care:</strong> Festive gift kits + Diwali beauty push.<br><strong>F&amp;B + specialty:</strong> Diwali gifting + festive hampers.<br><strong>Kids + baby:</strong> Festive + gifting + Diwali categories.<br><strong>Jewelry + accessories:</strong> Dhanteras adjacent + festive purchases.</p>
                                    <h2>Amazon Ads Strategy for GIS</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Sponsored Products:</strong> Aggressive bidding + budget increases 3-5x normal during GIS.<br><strong>Sponsored Brands:</strong> Store + brand visibility + festive banners.<br><strong>Sponsored Display:</strong> Retargeting + competitor targeting.<br><strong>Amazon Deals:</strong> Lightning Deals + Deal of the Day + Best Deals — apply weeks ahead.<br><strong>A+ Content updates:</strong> Festive-themed A+ content + comparison charts.<br><strong>Amazon Live:</strong> Live selling during GIS peak days.<br><strong>Subscribe &amp; Save promotion:</strong> Subscription attach lift for consumable categories.</p>
                                    <h2>Inventory + Ops Discipline</h2>
                                    <p>GIS demands operational excellence:<br><strong>Inventory 8-12 weeks ahead</strong> — stockouts during GIS destroy revenue + Amazon algorithm ranking.<br><strong>Fulfillment by Amazon (FBA) essential</strong> — Prime + faster delivery + eligibility for Deals.<br><strong>Amazon account manager coordination</strong> — deals approval + brand register + ecosystem support.<br><strong>Post-GIS return processing</strong> — high return volumes in fashion + electronics.</p>
                                    <h2>Ad Budget Concentration</h2>
                                    <p>GIS Amazon ad CPC inflation: 40-80% during peak days.<br><strong>Recommended allocation:</strong> pre-GIS (4-6 weeks): 25-35%. Peak GIS 4-7 days: 45-55%. Post-GIS Diwali extension: 15-25%.<br>GIS Amazon ad budget typically 40-60% of Q3 + Q4 Amazon ad total for participating brands.</p>

